#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065066} :activity/id #uuid "0ea01798-9472-5d12-99d8-c8fb5ac8d4e4" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050421 :topic/id #uuid "4786b31f-5de0-5307-bf80-b86cb35ed433" :topic/math-academy-id 328} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065066 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065358 :tutorial/content "Whenever we add a negative number, we write parentheses around the negative number so that it's easier to read. \n\nFor example, instead of\n\n$$\n7 + - 5\n$$\n\nwhich is difficult to read, we write\n\n$$\n7+(-5).\n$$\n\nAdding a negative number is the same as subtracting a positive number. Therefore, we can drop the addition sign and the parentheses in the above expression, which gives\n\n$$\n7 - 5.\n$$\n\nCarrying out the subtraction, as usual, we get \n\n$$\n7 - 5 = 2.\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "7bae60ac-f313-592d-89f9-3c81ca1f8ffd" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3024 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "ec6f2caa-f5b1-5075-9f11-533672bebafb" :step/math-academy-id 16371 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065067}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065067 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064211 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064073 :question/id #uuid "cecc0a5a-10be-59b9-a8c5-ae907679ed65" :question/math-academy-id "e-4474"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4851cda0-b113-5476-8e09-cceada5f07f6" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048549} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048911}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064574} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064921} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186444837} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186444839}] :knowledge-point/title "Adding a Negative Number"} :step/id #uuid "30bdc970-1e15-54e6-91ea-f689d47ff23a" :step/math-academy-id 16380 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065068}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065068 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064212 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064074 :question/id #uuid "f5138ecd-8e2e-5f83-a286-d770a53fba6f" :question/math-academy-id "e-4478"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "498454ca-7ef2-57fb-aa4b-4884aed0c24e" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048207}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064478} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064762} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186444840} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186444841}] :knowledge-point/title "Adding a Negative Decimal"} :step/id #uuid "ac43f3a6-1dd2-5c52-ad3b-ce55c1d1187b" :step/math-academy-id 16383 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065069}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065069 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065359 :tutorial/content "We can add a negative fraction using the same method. To demonstrate, let's find the value of\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2}{7} + \\left(- \\dfrac{5}{7}\\right).\n$$\n\nFirst, we eliminate the parentheses and obtain\n\n$$\n\\dfrac 2 {7} + \\left(-\\dfrac 5 {7}\\right) = \\dfrac 2 {7} -\\dfrac 5 {7}.\n$$\n\nNow, since both fractions have a common denominator of $7,$ we can combine the numerators, which gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{7}-\\frac{5}{7} & =\\frac{2-5}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we work out $2 - 5$ using our number line.\n\n![](images/c6/c63a3db44b79e751c7cf1a49dcebcbb1d00cea0427da4ef271d07646e4be2748.png)\n\nWe find that $2-5=-3.$ So, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac {2 - 5} {7} = \\dfrac{-3}{7} = -\\dfrac{3}{7}.\n$$\n\nIf two fractions have different denominators, we need to put them over a common denominator first and *then* subtract! Let's see an example." :tutorial/id #uuid "3edabc0b-b8c7-5264-aa38-ff64670a659b" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3030 :tutorial/title "Adding a Negative Fraction"} :step/id #uuid "0bc730cb-0417-5e76-aba1-3c7db86b1077" :step/math-academy-id 16388 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065070}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186065070 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064213 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064076 :question/id #uuid "aa932148-f7fc-5e12-ad35-e9e90df25cc6" :question/math-academy-id "e-4484"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd8feed5-e1ee-5d1a-bba3-4fb2adee27ed" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048639}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064765} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064766} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186444836} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186444838}] :knowledge-point/title "Adding a Negative Fraction"} :step/id #uuid "16791a41-5d92-5b62-943e-65117c5665dd" :step/math-academy-id 16398}] :activity/title "Adding a Negative Number" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186064419}]}
